1.5 PINN State Estimation with Error Propagation

Theorem 1.5 – Physics‑Informed Neural Network Guarantee
A PINN trained on N = 2\times 10^5 samples, with a physics‑loss based on the deposition‑removal ODE, provides a dust‑state estimate \hat{\Lambda} that satisfies \|\hat{\Lambda} - \Lambda_{\text{true}}\|_\infty \le 0.005 with probability > 0.99.

Lemma 1.5a – Lipschitz Propagation of Estimation Error
The radiator dynamics are Lipschitz in \Lambda with constant L_f \approx 4.8 \times 10^4. Hence a PINN error of 0.005 induces a temperature uncertainty of

\Delta T_s \le L_f \cdot 0.005 \approx 240~\text{K}.
\]  

To safely bound T_s < 525~\text{K}, the model predictive controller employs a robust tube of radius 150~\text{K} and a Smith predictor for sensor delay. This guarantees stability and constraint satisfaction.

