1.6 Synergistic Material Degradation

Theorem 1.6 – UV + Perchlorate Degradation of FEP
The rate of solar absorptance increase is

\frac{d\alpha_0}{dt} = k_{UV} I_{UV} + k_{Cl}[\text{ClO}_4^-] I_{UV},
\]  

where I_{UV} \approx 0.1~\text{W/m}^2 and perchlorate concentration in dust is \sim 0.5~\text{wt}\%. Accelerated testing shows k_{Cl}/k_{UV} \approx 8, reducing the degradation time constant from 3000 sols (UV only) to roughly 400 sols. End‑of‑mission \alpha_0 can reach 0.30–0.35. Therefore the variable‑emissivity electrochromic layer must cover 100 % of the radiator area to compensate for this degradation.

